{
  "mechanism": {
    "summary": "A token bucket keeps two fields per key in a shared store: a token count and the time of the last refill. Each request first refills the bucket for the time elapsed, capped at the capacity, then takes one token or is refused with HTTP 429 and a Retry-After header.",
    "sourceChunkIds": [
      "source-1#chunk-1"
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Build the key from the API key and the route group.",
        "sourceChunkIds": [
          "source-1#chunk-1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Read the key's token count and last-refill timestamp from the shared store.",
        "sourceChunkIds": [
          "source-1#chunk-1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the tokens earned since then (elapsed seconds times the refill rate), capped at the capacity.",
        "sourceChunkIds": [
          "source-1#chunk-1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "If a token is left, take it, write the count and timestamp back, and let the request through.",
        "sourceChunkIds": [
          "source-1#chunk-1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Otherwise answer 429, with Retry-After computed from the refill rate.",
        "sourceChunkIds": [
          "source-1#chunk-1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Steps 2 to 4 run as one atomic script inside the store, so two gateway nodes cannot both spend the last token.",
        "sourceChunkIds": [
          "source-1#chunk-2"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "fact-1",
      "statement": "A free-tier key at the example gateway gets a capacity of 100 tokens and refills at 10 tokens per second, so a quiet client can burst 100 requests and then settles to 10 per second.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-1"
      ],
      "confidence": "medium"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-2",
      "statement": "Without an atomic check-and-take, two gateway nodes can read the same count, both see one token left, and both admit a request.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-3",
      "statement": "If each of 24 gateway nodes kept its own bucket, a client spread across them would get 24 times its limit.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-4",
      "statement": "A fixed window that resets every minute lets a client send its quota at the end of one minute and again at the start of the next: up to 2 times the limit within two seconds.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-5",
      "statement": "A sliding window log is exact but stores one timestamp per request, so its memory grows with the limit.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-1"
      ],
      "confidence": "medium"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-6",
      "statement": "A sliding window counter keeps 2 counters per key and is approximate: it assumes the previous window's requests were evenly spread.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-1"
      ],
      "confidence": "medium"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-7",
      "statement": "quotaflow fails closed by default when the store fails, refusing with 503; its optional local fallback multiplies the effective limit by the number of instances.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-2"
      ],
      "confidence": "medium"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-8",
      "statement": "Taking timestamps inside the store makes the limiter immune to clock skew between instances.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-2"
      ],
      "confidence": "medium"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-9",
      "statement": "Larkspur Pay's checkout limiter failed open when its store slowed after a cross-zone failover, and each of its 40 instances enforced the full limit locally.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-3#chunk-1"
      ],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-10",
      "statement": "After the incident, the limiter for the payment provider fails closed and local fallback limits are divided by the number of instances.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-3#chunk-2"
      ],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact-11",
      "statement": "quotaflow claims accuracy within 0.5% of an ideal limiter under any load; the claim comes from its own README, with no measurement.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-1"
      ],
      "confidence": "low"
    }
  ],
  "numbers": [
    {
      "id": "num-1",
      "value": "100",
      "unit": "tokens",
      "context": "Token-bucket capacity of a free-tier key at the example gateway",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-1#chunk-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-2",
      "value": "10",
      "unit": "tokens per second",
      "context": "Refill rate of the same free-tier key",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-1#chunk-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-3",
      "value": "24",
      "unit": "gateway nodes",
      "context": "Gateway nodes behind the example gateway's load balancer",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-1#chunk-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-4",
      "value": "0.4",
      "unit": "ms",
      "context": "Median round trip to the shared store, paid on every request",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-1#chunk-2",
      "asOf": "June 2024"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-5",
      "value": "2.1",
      "unit": "ms",
      "context": "p99 round trip to the shared store, paid on every request",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-1#chunk-2",
      "asOf": "June 2024"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-6",
      "value": "2",
      "unit": "times the limit",
      "context": "Worst-case burst of a per-minute fixed window around the window boundary",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-1#chunk-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-7",
      "value": "2 million",
      "unit": "requests per second",
      "context": "A flood that still reaches the gateways before any limiter can refuse it",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-1#chunk-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-8",
      "value": "8",
      "unit": "bytes per timestamp",
      "context": "Memory per stored request in a sliding window log",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-2#chunk-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-9",
      "value": "8 KB",
      "unit": "per active key",
      "context": "Sliding window log memory at a limit of 1,000 requests per minute",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-2#chunk-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-10",
      "value": "4 GB",
      "unit": "",
      "context": "Sliding window log memory for 500,000 active keys at that limit",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-2#chunk-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-11",
      "value": "50",
      "unit": "ms",
      "context": "quotaflow's default store timeout; slower calls count as store failures",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-2#chunk-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-12",
      "value": "47",
      "unit": "minutes",
      "context": "Duration of Larkspur Pay's checkout incident",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-3#chunk-1",
      "asOf": "14 March 2025"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-13",
      "value": "31%",
      "unit": "of checkout requests",
      "context": "Share of checkout requests that failed during the incident",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-3#chunk-1",
      "asOf": "14 March 2025"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-14",
      "value": "80",
      "unit": "ms",
      "context": "Store call latency after the failover, up from about 1 ms",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-3#chunk-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-15",
      "value": "300",
      "unit": "requests per second",
      "context": "Larkspur Pay's contracted rate with its payment provider",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-3#chunk-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "num-16",
      "value": "150",
      "unit": "ms",
      "context": "New store timeout for the checkout limiter, up from 50 ms, above a cross-zone round trip",
      "sourceChunkId": "source-3#chunk-2"
    }
  ],
  "tradeOffs": [
    {
      "choice": "Keep every bucket in one shared in-memory store",
      "gains": "Every gateway node enforces the same limit, so 24 nodes do not multiply it.",
      "costs": "A network round trip on every request: 0.4 ms at the median, 2.1 ms at p99.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Token bucket",
      "gains": "Bursts are bounded by the capacity wherever the clock is.",
      "costs": "Two fields per key, updated by an atomic script in the store on every request.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2",
        "source-2#chunk-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Fail closed when the store fails",
      "gains": "The limiter never serves traffic it cannot count, so a downstream contract limit holds.",
      "costs": "A slow store refuses or delays requests that would have been fine.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-2",
        "source-3#chunk-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Sliding window counter",
      "gains": "Only 2 counters per key, whatever the limit.",
      "costs": "Approximate: it assumes the previous window's requests were evenly spread.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-1"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "rejectedAlternatives": [
    {
      "alternative": "A fixed window counter per calendar minute",
      "reason": "Cheap, one counter per key, but a client can send its whole quota at the end of one minute and again at the start of the next: up to 2 times the limit in two seconds.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "alternative": "A separate bucket on each gateway node",
      "reason": "A client spread across 24 nodes would get 24 times its limit.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "misconceptions": [
    {
      "belief": "A rate limiter protects a service from a flood of traffic.",
      "correction": "It keeps well-behaved clients fair. A flood of 2 million requests per second still reaches the gateways, which must parse each request before refusing it; dropping floods is the network edge's job.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "failureModes": [
    {
      "kind": "incident",
      "description": "A cross-zone failover slowed store calls from about 1 ms to 80 ms, past the 50 ms timeout. The limiter failed open, each of 40 instances allowed the full limit, and traffic to the payment provider reached roughly 40 times the contracted 300 requests per second. The provider throttled everything: 31% of checkouts failed for 47 minutes.",
      "incident": {
        "date": "14 March 2025",
        "publisher": "Larkspur Pay platform team"
      },
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-3#chunk-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "failure_mode",
      "description": "Without an atomic script, two nodes read the same count and both spend the last token, letting extra requests through.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "edge_case",
      "description": "A local fallback while the store is down multiplies the effective limit by the number of instances unless each local limit is divided by it.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-2",
        "source-3#chunk-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "edge_case",
      "description": "Keys are kept until 2 windows after their last request, so memory for idle keys lingers.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-2"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "hooks": [
    {
      "situation": "Your limiter allows 300 requests per second. One slow store later, each of 40 instances allows the full limit on its own.",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-3#chunk-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "situation": "100 tokens, 10 per second, 24 gateway nodes: where does the bucket live so the limit holds?",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-1",
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "situation": "A fixed window lets a client send 2 times its quota inside two seconds. How?",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-1#chunk-2"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "openQuestions": [
    {
      "question": "Should a limiter fail open or closed when its store fails? quotaflow recommends fail closed for every route; Larkspur Pay chose fail open for checkout and is still undecided for its own APIs.",
      "reason": "disagreement",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-2",
        "source-3#chunk-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How accurate is a sliding window counter in practice? The only figure is quotaflow's own claim of within 0.5%, with no measurement behind it.",
      "reason": "not_covered",
      "sourceChunkIds": [
        "source-2#chunk-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What capacity and refill rate suit paid tiers? The sources give only the free tier.",
      "reason": "not_covered",
      "sourceChunkIds": []
    }
  ]
}
